# The diagnostic tools answer this Mac only, whatever the exposure selector in
# the app says. Opening Apache to the local network is meant to show a project
# on a phone, not to hand phpinfo() (paths, environment, every ini value), the
# listening ports with their processes, the file listing of the projects and
# the phpMyAdmin frame to whoever is on the same wifi. phpMyAdmin itself is
# already "Require local" in httpd-vxost.conf: this brings the four dashboard
# tools under the same rule. From this Mac nothing changes.
#
# ⚠️ Case-insensitive, (?i): the macOS filesystem is case-insensitive, so
# PHPINFO.php and Phpinfo.php are the same file, and a rule that only knew the
# lowercase spelling let them through. And it sits HERE, not in the root
# .htaccess: a rule on the file name at the root also blocked
# /projects/<site>/database.php, which is a perfectly ordinary endpoint of a
# project. browse.php is reached as DirectoryIndex of /projects/: the
# subrequest passes through this folder and the rule applies to it too.
<FilesMatch "(?i)^(phpinfo|ports|browse|database)\.php$">
    Require local
</FilesMatch>
